  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fast-Track Transportation from Moldova to Romania in Support of Authorities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">After eight years of armed conflict in eastern Ukraine, which had left millions of people in need of humanitarian assistance, the Russian Federation launched a military offensive on the country on 24 February 2022. This has triggered one of the fastest-growing displacement and humanitarian crises on record, pushing millions into internal displacement and abroad in search of safety. The Republic of Moldova is one of the countries most affected by the refugee situation, and its border, migration and asylum management capacities are under significant strain. Some 75 per cent of refugees arriving to Moldova continue towards Romania and other European countries, nonetheless the proportion that remains is straining the country&apos;s capacity. As part of burden sharing between the receiving countries, it is the priority of the UN and governments involved to assist refugees with onward transportation, primarily to Romania by road and rail, and to the European Union (EU+) countries by air. Through this project, IOM seeks to provide refugees from Ukraine with safe and dignified transportation from Palanca border crossing point between Ukraine and Moldova, to Romanian border and further to Bucharest, where refugees can either stay or proceed to other EU member states by road or train.</narrative>
  </description>
